==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Compound of {{com|en|tax|haven}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{l|en|law|business|taxation}} A [[jurisdiction]] that [[levy|levies]] low tax rates on certain economic activities, especially to attract wealthy individuals and ([[foreign]]) [[business]]es.
#* {{quote-web|en|url=http://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2013/aug/14/gibraltar-falklands-deny-logic-history|title=Gibraltar and the Falklands deny the logic of history|author=Simon Jenkins|date=2013-08-14|work=The Guardian|passage=Such colonies claim to be "more British than the British", except that they pay no UK tax and act as '''tax havens''' for funds from Britain. Gibraltar has made a particular specialism of internet gambling.}}

